          "en": "Instructor: We added the header in the last lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "Now I want to work on my recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 11.94,
          "en": "So we get the RecipesComponent which holds the recipe list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.94,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "Now I also want to fill the list with some life.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "For this I'll go into my RecipeListComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "and we will learn more about ngOnInut later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.54,
          "en": "in the next module, in the components module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 25.65,
          "en": "For now what I want to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 28.23,
          "en": "is I want to add my recipes array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 31.68,
          "en": "My array of recipes, which for now is an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.68,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "And here, let's go back to that slide from the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "I want to define how a recipe should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "We're going to use a recipe a lot throughout this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "and therefore we should definitely clearly define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 48.33,
          "en": "how a recipe looks like so that whenever we use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 50.67,
          "en": "in any component, we're always talking about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "the same structure, about the same kind of object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "So for this, I will create a model. What is a model then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "A model simply is a TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "So in the recipes folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 64.074,
          "en": "because it's going to be the recipe model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.074,
          "end": 69.074,
          "en": "I'll add another file. It's called recipe.model.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.814,
          "end": 73.44,
          "en": "Now .model is optional, but again you should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "be descriptive about what's inside a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 78.408,
          "en": "And with that, it's pretty clear what will be inside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.408,
          "end": 80.28,
          "en": "So I'll add this file again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "It's now just in the recipes folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.89,
          "en": "And how should this file look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.89,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "First of all, I'm going to export a TS class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 91.923,
          "en": "a TypeScript class which is simply named Recipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "Because we define how a single recipe looks like here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 99.187,
          "en": "Now you could think that we're going to add something like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.187,
          "end": 101.64,
          "en": "@Model here, and we're not going to do this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.64,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "there is no decorator like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "And we don't need to do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "because we can use vanilla TypeScript for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.3,
          "end": 111.583,
          "en": "A model in the end should just be a blueprint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.583,
          "end": 113.82,
          "en": "for objects we create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.82,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "And a TypeScript class does just this job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "A class can be instantiated, so we can create new objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "based on the setup we provide here in this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 128.583,
          "en": "So we can define how a recipe should look like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.583,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "in this class. So let's do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 136.26,
          "en": "A recipe should have a name, and I'll add an accessor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.26,
          "end": 139.11,
          "en": "to be really clear about that this is publicly available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.11,
          "end": 142.57,
          "en": "so that this can be accessed from outside if using this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.57,
          "end": 144.435,
          "en": "as an instantiated object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.435,
          "end": 146.97,
          "en": "So I'll add public in front of it and then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.97,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "name as the property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.55,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "I'll also assign the type of this by adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.86,
          "en": "and the type will be string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.86,
          "end": 157.44,
          "en": "And that is just how you assign types in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "You add a colon after the property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 161.46,
          "en": "and then the type you want to assign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 163.173,
          "en": "So string in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "I also want to have a description in each recipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "So I'll add my description property, which also is a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 175.383,
          "en": "because a description is just a text of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.55,
          "end": 181.55,
          "en": "Now maybe we also want to store a image for each recipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "So we should have a imagePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "since we won't store the image itself here of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 191.76,
          "en": "that wouldn't work. We can't store files in our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.76,
          "end": 194.79,
          "en": "but we want to store the path pointing to the image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.79,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "And we will simply use images from the web here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.16,
          "end": 199.38,
          "en": "So this will hold a URL in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 202.8,
          "en": "So that is also a string, a text in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 207.69,
          "en": "That is the basic model for now. The basic blueprint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.69,
          "end": 209.82,
          "en": "I'll also add a constructor to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.82,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "so that we can instantiate this with the new keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 215.06900000000002,
          "en": "and pass the arguments right to the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.06900000000002,
          "end": 218.28,
          "en": "So here I expect to receive the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 219.84,
          "en": "which will be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.84,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "The description, I'll just write it a bit shorter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 224.46,
          "en": "which will be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.46,
          "end": 228.12,
          "en": "And the imagePath, which will be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.12,
          "end": 231.27,
          "en": "In the constructor body, and if that's brand new to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.27,
          "end": 233.49,
          "en": "the constructor assembly's a built-in function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.49,
          "end": 235.986,
          "en": "every class has and which will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.986,
          "end": 239.13,
          "en": "once you create a new instance of this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.13,
          "end": 241.53,
          "en": "I will show you how this works in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.53,
          "end": 243.406,
          "en": "So inside of the body of this constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.406,
          "end": 246.052,
          "en": "we have to assign the arguments we receive here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.052,
          "end": 248.63,
          "en": "to the properties of our object now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.63,
          "end": 250.005,
          "en": "to the properties of our class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.005,
          "end": 253.02,
          "en": "So this name referring to the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.02,
          "end": 256.95,
          "en": "up here to our property should be equal to name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.95,
          "end": 259.14,
          "en": "And now the same for description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.14,
          "end": 261.51,
          "en": "this description should be equal to desc",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.51,
          "end": 264.93,
          "en": "and this imagePath should be equal to imagePath.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.93,
          "end": 267.96,
          "en": "So if then we got a recipe model we can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.96,
